lootmap shows what an infostealer or a Shai-Hulud style worm would take
from this computer, and helps you lock it down.

lootmap never uses the network by default and never prints secret values.

Usage:
  lootmap [flags]
  lootmap [command]

Available Commands:
  check-packages Check lockfiles and package caches for known malicious OSV MAL- versions
  doctor         Show the environment and which probes would run
  explain        Explain a finding and how to remediate or rotate it
  fix            Preview, back up, and apply safe remediations
  help           Help about any command
  scan           Scan this computer for exposed credentials and build a loot map
  undo           Restore files from the most recent or specified backup snapshot
  update-db      Download and verify the latest signed OSV MAL- advisory bundle (uses network)

Flags:
  -h, --help      help for lootmap
  -v, --version   version for lootmap

Use "lootmap [command] --help" for more information about a command.
